.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-2-Clause
.Dd October 11, 2026
.Dt NETWORK_STATE 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm network_state_open ,
.Nm network_state_watch ,
.Nm network_state_close
.Nd observe sampled network interface state
.Sh LIBRARY
.Li libnetworkcmp
.Pq Fl lnetworkcmp
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In network_state.h
.Ft int
.Fn network_state_open "struct network_state_client **client"
.Ft int
.Fn network_state_watch "struct network_state_client *client" "struct network_state_snapshot *snapshot" "uint32_t timeout_ms"
.Ft void
.Fn network_state_close "struct network_state_client *client"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
These functions observe the latest interface inventory from
.Va system.Network.State .
The caller needs the approved software attribute
.Va system.network.observe
and session right
.Dv NETWORK_STATE_RIGHT_READ .
No kernel token or network socket is returned.
.Pp
.Fn network_state_open
opens a session.
.Fn network_state_watch
returns the initial snapshot immediately, then waits for a changed snapshot.
Identical samples are suppressed and intermediate changes may be coalesced.
The snapshot contains nonzero epoch and generation values, a
.Va source_error ,
and up to 256 interface records sorted by index.
Each record contains index, name, flags, MTU, and link state
(unknown, down, or up).
No addresses or packet counters are exposed.
Names are byte strings; escape control bytes before terminal output.
.Pp
A nonzero
.Va source_error
is an errno value indicating unavailable source data;
.Va count
is then zero.
This is a successful observation, not a failed watch or an empty inventory.
The initial source error may be
.Er EAGAIN
before the first sample finishes.
Recovery produces another snapshot.
.Pp
BSDNetwork samples BSDSysctl's read-only interface inventory approximately
one second after each completed read.
This is neither an event history nor proof of Internet connectivity.
Interface fields are not an atomic snapshot across all interfaces.
Compare generations only within the same epoch.
Reconnects and provider restarts establish a fresh observation cursor.
.Pp
A zero timeout polls; a finite timeout is in milliseconds.
.Dv NETWORK_STATE_TIMEOUT_INFINITE
waits without a watch deadline.
An unchanged snapshot at the deadline returns
.Er EAGAIN .
The transport adds a five-second allowance to finite watch deadlines,
saturating below the infinite value.
.Pp
The client speaks the
.Sy NetworkState
protocol of the FIDL library
.Sy bsd.network.v1
.Pq Pa /usr/share/fidl/networkcmp.fidl ;
see
.Xr fidl 7 .
Each new session first negotiates the wire version
.Pq Er EPROTONOSUPPORT .
The provider applies the record rules of the earlier wire format: indices
strictly increasing, names one to fifteen bytes without NUL and unique,
link state at most up, and no records with a source error.
.Fn network_state_validate_request
and
.Fn network_state_validate_reply
.Pq In network_state_protocol.h
check the pre-FIDL records and are kept for compatibility.
.Pp
Calls on a client are serialized.
Only one watch may be outstanding per session.
The provider allows 128 sessions, at most 16 per authenticated label,
and closes sessions idle between requests for 30 seconds.
Pending watches are governed by their watch deadline instead.
.Pp
.Fn network_state_close
releases the client; callers must first finish concurrent calls.
A client inherited across fork cannot be used in the child.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
Open and watch return zero on success or minus one with
.Va errno
set on failure.
Watch leaves the caller's snapshot unchanged on failure.
A validated server timeout preserves the session.
Transport or protocol failures discard it; the next call attempts to reopen,
and receives a fresh initial snapshot.
The failed call is never silently retried.
.Sh ERRORS
.Bl -tag -width Er
.It Bq Er EAGAIN
No change before the watch deadline.
.It Bq Er ECHILD
The client belongs to the parent process.
.It Bq Er EPROTO
Malformed reply.
.It Bq Er ETIMEDOUT
Transport deadline expired.
.El
Discovery, authorization, allocation, and channel errors are also returned.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr libnetworkcmp 3 ,
.Xr sysctlcmp_interfaces 3 ,
.Xr fidl 7 ,
.Xr BSDNetwork 8 ,
.Xr networkcmpctl 8
